Dear QA Team,

I am writing on behalf of City Pharmacy Chain to report a packaging defect found in a
recent shipment of Amoxicillin 250mg Capsules, Batch Number AMX-0721.

Manufacturing Date: 18-11-2024
Expiry Date: 17-11-2026

Out of 5 boxes (approximately 12 kg total) received at our Pune outlet, 2 boxes had blister
strips with broken seals, exposing capsules to ambient air. Several capsules in the affected
strips appeared to have absorbed moisture and were slightly discolored (pale yellow instead
of the usual white). Customers have not yet consumed the affected stock; we withdrew it
immediately upon inspection.

This was first noticed by our store pharmacist, Priya Sharma, during shelf restocking on
14th September 2026. Given the potential moisture ingress and efficacy risk to patients if
dispensed, we are treating this as a high-priority issue and would appreciate your team's
immediate assessment.

Please advise on next steps and let us know if you require the affected units returned for
investigation.

Regards,
Priya Sharma
Store Manager, City Pharmacy Chain - Pune
